# D'Agriventory Project Context

This document provides a global context for the D'Agriventory project, an inventory management system designed for agricultural purposes.

## Technology Stack

The project is built on the TALL stack with some modern additions:

-   **Backend**: [PHP 8.2](mdc:https:/www.php.net) & [Laravel 12](mdc:https:/laravel.com)
-   **Frontend**: [Livewire](mdc:https:/livewire.laravel.com) with [Volt](mdc:https:/livewire.laravel.com/docs/volt) for single-file components.
-   **UI**: [Tailwind CSS 4](mdc:https:/tailwindcss.com) & [Blade](mdc:https:/laravel.com/docs/12.x/blade) templates.
-   **Asset Bundling**: [Vite](mdc:https:/vitejs.dev)
-   **Testing**: [Pest](mdc:https:/pestphp.com)

## Core Domain Models

The application's domain revolves around inventory management. Key models (and their corresponding tables) include:

-   **Users & Roles**: `users`, `admin_users`, `employees`, `positions`
-   **Organization**: `divisions`, `suppliers`
-   **Procurement**: `contracts`, `contract_items`
-   **Inventory Catalog**: `primary_categories`, `secondary_categories`, `items_catalog`, `item_specifications`
-   **Inventory Items**: `consumable_items`
-   **Tracking & Transfers**: `ics_number`, `par_number`, `idr_number`, `ics_transfers`, `par_transfers`
-   **Auditing**: `audit_logs`

## Development Workflow

-   **Code Generation**: Use `php artisan make:*` commands to create new classes.
-   **Development Server**: Run `composer run dev` to start the local server, queue listener, and Vite dev server concurrently.
-   **Testing**: Run tests using `composer test`.




